    "lawCode": "Amd §66, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9122\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to directing the\npublic service commission to develop, publish, and update a guidebook on\nthe gas and electric ratemaking process\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to facilitate participation in, and promote\npublic understanding of, the electric and gas ratemaking process.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Requires the Public Service Commission (PSC) to develop,\npublish, and update a guidebook which provides practical information\nrelating to the electric and gas ratemaking process. The guidebook must\nbe written in plain language, accessible to the general public, and\ncontain specific information for public participation and for interven-\ning parties.\n\nSection 2: Requires that the guidebook be published within 120 days of\nthis act becoming law.\n\nSection 3: Establishes an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe electric and gas ratemaking process is a complicated, technical, and\nsometimes opaque process which is of increasingly important significance\nas utility rates have begun to rise. The current process is guided by a\ncombination of statutory and regulatory requirements as well as PSC\norders, rules, and guidelines. Participating in this process can be a\ndaunting task for both the general public and parties interested in\nintervening and formally taking part. Parties which may be interested in\nintervening may be dissuaded from actually participating given that\nhelpful information and guidance about this process can be hard to come\nby. This bill is an important step in making the details of this compli-\ncated process more accessible and easily understood.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
